--TEST--
`Core\Request::cookie` answers the same way for every name it is given when no request arrived, so neither a prefix nor a spelling reaches the decision -- ADR 0012 § 7, `rule:errors/cookie-name-bytes`, spec § 15
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Invariance over a sweep, counted rather than read off a line. A cookie name
// is bytes and nothing is substituted in either direction, so the four
// spellings below are four different cookies -- and `__Host-` carries a rule of
// its own about what is visible. None of that is reached here: whether a
// request arrived is decided before the name is looked at, so a member that
// answered `null` for one spelling and refused for another would be telling a
// caller which cookies a request it never received did not carry.
uint $refused = 0;
try {
    Core\Request::cookie("session");
} catch (LogicError $ordinary) {
    $refused = $refused + 1;
}
try {
    Core\Request::cookie("__Host-session");
} catch (LogicError $hosted) {
    $refused = $refused + 1;
}
try {
    Core\Request::cookie("__Secure-session");
} catch (LogicError $secured) {
    $refused = $refused + 1;
}
try {
    Core\Request::cookie("a.b");
} catch (LogicError $dotted) {
    $refused = $refused + 1;
}
try {
    Core\Request::cookie("a_b");
} catch (LogicError $scored) {
    $refused = $refused + 1;
}
try {
    Core\Request::cookie("");
} catch (LogicError $empty) {
    $refused = $refused + 1;
}
echo "every name refused: ", $refused, " of 6\n";

// And the message names the member rather than the name, which is the counted
// claim stated the other way: no spelling of a cookie can be told from another
// by reading it.
try {
    Core\Request::cookie("__Host-session");
} catch (LogicError $why) {
    echo $why->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
every name refused: 6 of 6
Core\Request::cookie(): there is no request here — this program is not answering one, as a CLI program, a scheduled script, a job worker and a test are not. That is refused rather than answered empty, because "no request arrived" and "the request sent nothing" are different facts
